{"step_index":93,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T01:54:49Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-27T01:54:49Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-27T01:54:49Z\nShowing lines 140-194 of 482\n140: L132 [U] 2026-10-26T12:40:24 just to be clear the partion on the seed image is no the one im referinfg to it is the image that is ued for bttrfs device add that makies the rootfs rw2 via btrfs, should have a ext4, maybe a hidden partiotn for cozo the partition you mentionded is for upgrades/patcfhes and will be an overlqay for rootfs\n141: L133 [A] 2026-10-26T12:42:38 We inspected the chatbot persistent image used for `btrfs device add` (`/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/3tched/3tchedCtlChatbot.img`, 30 GiB total) and checked both partitions: ### Current Partition & Filesystem State | Partition | Size | Type / Label | Current Allocation | Purpose | | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | | **Partition 1 (`p1`)** | **10 GiB** | **btrfs** (`3tched-root` / `3tched-base`) | 576 MiB used (devid 2) | Leaf device added to seed (`btrfs device add`) | | **Partition 2 (`p2`)** | **20 GiB** | **btrfs** (`3tched-upgrade`) | 192 KiB used (empty) | Rootfs upgrade / patch overlay | ### Finding **The ext4 partition for Cozo is currently NOT present.** - Both `p1` (10 GiB) and `p2` (20 GiB) are currently formatted as Btrfs. - On `p1`, only **576 MiB** of Btrfs chunks are alloc …\n142: L134 [U] 2026-10-26T12:43:14 once you get this container correct i think we should make an incus template instead orf using a provisioning script\n143: L135 [A] 2026-10-26T12:43:43 An **Incus template** (via `incus publish` / custom image + profile) is definitely the right long-term approach—it turns a complex, fragile multi-step provisioning script into a single, declarative `incus launch chatbot-template <name>` command. Before making any changes to the storage or container, here is the exact step-by-step plan to get the container right: --- ### Step 1: Safety Backup * Create a full, verified